 text=[]
 text.append('# Stage 7 fixed-k4 spatial validation decision — 2026-10-10\n')
 text.append('This is a bounded exploratory validation of two already specified, equal-five-domain, four-class models. It is not a new feature search, k search, formal Stage7 replacement, or causal analysis. Parent commit: `'+PARENT+'`. Exactly40 new KMeans fits reuse the20 existing deletion sets, same seeds42–61, n_init100, and the same2,287 complete residential tracts. All2,291 original residential records remain in the source table; four unresolved geometry cases receive no imputation or labels. No source acquisition or physical/recovery/GA calculation was performed.\n')
 text.append('## Overall partition sensitivity\n')
 rows=[]
 for model,v in modelsummary.items():rows.append(dict(model=model,full_ARI_median=v['full_ARI']['median'],full_ARI_p05=v['full_ARI']['p05'],full_ARI_min=v['full_ARI']['minimum'],training_ARI_median=v['training_ARI']['median'],heldout_ARI_median=v['heldout_ARI']['median'],changed_n_median=v['changed_tract_n']['median'],changed_n_max=v['changed_tract_n']['maximum']))
 text.append(pd.DataFrame(rows).to_markdown(index=False,floatfmt='.4f')+'\n')
 text.append('ARI is chance-adjusted partition agreement, not the percentage classified correctly. Ranges across these20 fixed spatial perturbations are descriptive, not confidence intervals or independent validation. All comparisons use each seed own saved full-data k4 labels. Seed42 alignment is for presentation only. Label matching uses retained training tracts and is not reoptimized on heldout tracts. Full/training/heldout cross-tables remain available to show splitting and mixing hidden by an assigned name. No numerical pass threshold was chosen after seeing these results.\n')
 text.append('## Six required scientific judgments\n')
 text.append('**1. D maintains its main groups in most tested deletions, with a concrete weak case.** Its three large display groups have median Jaccard values shown below. Worst D seed54 changes225 tract assignments after training-based alignment; that is9.84% of2,287 records, distinct from its ARI0.7522. This is not wholesale loss of all group structure, but it is too substantial to call geographic membership invariant.\n')
 cc=pd.DataFrame(classsummary);cc=cc.loc[cc.scope.eq('full'),['model','display_seed42_cluster','retention_median','retention_minimum','purity_median','purity_minimum','jaccard_median','jaccard_minimum','majority_incoming_count']]
 text.append(cc.to_markdown(index=False,floatfmt='.4f')+'\n')
 text.append('**2. Lower-tail agreement is associated with particular geographic deletions, not simply how many records are removed.** D lowest run is seed54, removing blocks7:-23 and7:-24 (480 records). Seed45 removes498 yet has ARI0.8318; the largest deletion, seed48 (534), has ARI0.8682. Identical sets can recur under different seeds:42/47 and53/57, for example. They remain20 prescribed algorithm/deletion cases, not20 unique independent geographic experiments. BASELINE_CLASS_SPATIAL_SUPPORT.csv and the run cross-tables identify exactly which baseline communities occupy each block.\n')
 text.append('Lowest runs in each model:\n')
 text.append(r.sort_values('full_ARI').groupby('model',sort=False).head(5)[['model','seed','removed_blocks','n_training','n_heldout','full_ARI','aligned_changed_n']].to_markdown(index=False,floatfmt='.4f')+'\n')
 text.append('**3. The34-member group never lacks training support and never loses its original members, but can be strongly contaminated.** D seed42 zero-based NPZ label1 (displayC2) is identified from saved membership, not hard-coded. EAL seed42 independently has the same34 members (its other groups differ). Each deletion leaves4–34 of those members in training. All34 are retained in the corresponding full-population predicted class in every run. However, deleting7:-23/7:-24 leaves only4 training members; the D matched class expands to92 with58 incoming records (purity34/92=0.3696), and EAL to90 with56 incoming (purity0.3778). Therefore there are zero no-training-support cases; the weakness is dilution despite remaining support, not disappearance or forced preservation. Every raw cross-table and original-member destination count is retained.\n')
 smalltable=p.loc[p.seed.eq(54)&p.display_seed42_cluster.eq(2)&p.profile_population.eq('reclassified_matched_full_population')&p.feature.isin(['B_480_hr','Init_Supply','SOVI_SCORE']),['model','feature','baseline_mean','mean','mean_change_standardized_full_cohort']]
 text.append(smalltable.to_markdown(index=False,floatfmt='.6f')+'\n')
 text.append('These values show substantive composition change: D small-group mean service loss rises from23.601 to29.111h, and Init_Supply falls from0.018153 to0.010640. Init_Supply is modeled normalized initial availability, not delivered electricity. The4-member retained-training subset and the92-member reassigned class are separate profiles, so deletion-induced compositional change is not confused with reassignment. The high-initial-service/low-service-loss description persists in relative direction, but exact size, membership specificity and magnitudes require qualification.\n')
 text.append('**4. EAL has higher agreement on these same cases, but shares the small-group weakness.** Its median full ARI0.9458 and minimum0.8666 exceed D0.9234 and0.7522; this is evidence about this fixed spatial design, not a scientific reason to collapse economic stock and loss propensity into one variable. EAL has the same34-member special group, while seed42 large classes are718/919/616 rather than D850/651/752. They are not interchangeable community taxonomies.\n')
 text.append('**5. Most reassignment occurs near descriptive class boundaries, with an important class-meaning exception.** Distance margins use full-data standardized/weighted distances to saved-label member means; the original full-data KMeans centers were not saved. They are not recovered algorithm decision margins or probabilities.\n')
 btable=[]
