 text.append('Do not turn differences such as EAL C1/C3 service-loss ranking (6/20 reversals) into stable archetype labels. D C1/C4 degree and network-impact rankings reverse12/20 times; EAL C2/C3 age ranking reverses9/20 times. A direction change with a tiny baseline effect should not be equated with a wholesale semantic reversal; both signed standardized magnitude and membership diagnostics must be read together.\n')
 text.append('## Profile definitions and limitations\n')
 text.append('SPATIAL_K4_PROFILE_STABILITY.csv separately records(A) retained original-class training members,(B) the matched predicted class on all2,287 tracts, and(C) the matched predicted training class. It reports mean/median/p10/p90/observedN/zero fraction, raw mean changes and changes in units of the full-cohort SD. Training total mean change decomposes into original-member deletion change plus reclassification change. Center shifts use a common full-baseline coordinate system with sqrt(0.2/domain coordinate count) weights, not changing training-scale coordinates. T80, population density and housing5+ are descriptions only. Profile quantiles describe members, not confidence intervals.\n')
 text.append('Original baseline matrix and sample hashes reproduce exactly. Some saved full-data algorithm inertias are slightly higher than inertia about final-label means (each discrepancy is recorded in INPUT_AND_BASELINE_QA.json). This is consistent with tolerance stopping followed by final label reassignment; original centers were not saved, so the exact earlier stopping path cannot be verified. No complete baseline was refitted to erase that distinction. All new perturbations save their actual scaler mean/variance/scale, factors, KMeans centers, raw labels, baseline labels, train mask, IDs, parameters and software versions.\n')
 text.append('## Recommendation and adoption gates\n')
 text.append('Both fixed-k4 models can enter manuscript integration review with the complete class-level and spatial limitations disclosed. This is not approval for final adoption or label replacement. D remains the provisional construct-driven specification because separate building stock and unadjusted multi-hazard loss propensity are interpretable; EAL is a compact combined expected-loss/exposure sensitivity. This choice is not an ARI/silhouette/VIF ranking. SOVI, Init_Supply and original model definitions are retained.\n')
 text.append('Substantive remaining issues are(1) geographic contamination of the34-member class under sparse training support,(2) fine feature/order descriptions that reverse,(3) inherited measurement uncertainty in unclassified SCAG land and missing-age area,(4) explicit2,287 complete-case rather than2,291 full-label accounting. The last four mask cases were not a launch condition and are not recalculated here. Author review must decide whether the documented complete-case domain and qualified group descriptions are acceptable. Do not claim an invariant four-community taxonomy, unique optimal k, independent final validation, or causal built-environment effects. No algorithm, variable, weight or extra run was added to try to pass.\n')
