 (OUT/'README.md').write_text('# Fixed-k4 spatial validation\n\nStart with STAGE7_K4_DECISION_NOTE.md. Statistical reference is each seed own saved baseline; seed42 is display only. Exactly40 spatial fits, no full-baseline or k-search fits.\n\nSPATIAL_K4_RUNS: overall/training/heldout agreement and exact deletion sets.\nSPATIAL_K4_CLUSTER_MATCHING: training-only matching and class-level membership by scope.\nSPATIAL_K4_CROSSTABS: all raw overlap cells, including splits/mixtures.\nSPATIAL_K4_PROFILE_STABILITY: original-member deletion versus reassigned membership, original-unit profiles.\nSMALL_CLUSTER_34_AUDIT: original34 and independently identified EAL smallest group.\nrun_records: complete saved scalers, centers, feature weights, labels and specs.\n\nNull heldout class metrics mean that class has no members in that scope; null matching is reserved for no training support. No label is assigned to the four unresolved source records. Cluster IDs are arbitrary.\n',encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
 (OUT/'EXECUTION_LOG.md').write_text('# Execution record\n\n1. Checked original branch/HEAD and862 staged additions; saved logical index and protected hashes.\n2. Verified exact actual-byte input hashes against50df104; reconstructed existing weighted matrices/sample identities and read all40 saved baseline partitions. No baseline fit.\n3. Reused20 prescribed spatial sets and fitted D/EAL fixedk4 once perseed,40 total. Saved all actual scaler/center/prediction arrays.\n4. Repaired a new-script syntax error and a baseline inertia check before any fits. The inertia audit distinguishes label-mean centers from original unsaved algorithm centers.\n5. Corrected string-array encoding in own completed checkpoints without changing any numerical arrays; no fit repeated.\n6. Computed training-only Hungarian assignment, raw cross-tables, class flows, original-unit profiles, center changes, direction reversals, and small-group contamination.\n7. All additional summaries/tests use saved predictions; no more clustering calls.\n8. Scoped separate-branch commit and remote LFS read-back recorded by publish_k4.py.\n',encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
